{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_5cd17bb8-9fae-4451-8d31-ea30263f4e19","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a08f65868bb631d5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8/20260915T150443Z-6b7d597b/runs/specialist/38272543d24d40a5ad7455d3b42904f2/wt2/pkg/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/scaled_mm/emulation.py","content":"# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project\n\n\"\"\"FP8 w8a8 dense-linear emulation for AMD GPUs without hardware FP8.\n\n``torch._scaled_mm`` hard-rejects FP8 inputs on ROCm devices older than MI300\n(\"torch._scaled_mm is only supported on CUDA devices with compute capability\n>= 9.0 or 8.9, or ROCm MI300+\"). CDNA1/CDNA2 parts (gfx908 / gfx90a, e.g.\nMI250X) have no FP8 matrix instruction at all, so *no* scaled-mm provider can\nserve an FP8 checkpoint there. Before this kernel existed, the pre-MI300 ROCm\nFP8 registry fell through the aiter / skinny-GEMM / rowwise gates (all correctly\narch-gated) and landed on ``ChannelWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel``, whose\n``compute capability >= 89`` gate is fooled by gfx90a reporting capability\n``(9, 0)`` -- so the engine aborted inside ``profile_run``.\n\nThis kernel bridges the gap: it dequantizes the FP8 weight to the activation\ndtype ONCE at load time and then runs a plain ``F.linear``. That is the same\nrecipe already used in-tree by\n\n* ``model_executor/layers/quantization/fp8.py`` -- the ``VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT``\n  per-tensor / per-channel path (\"dequant to BF16 and run GEMM\"), and\n* ``model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/emulation.py`` --\n  ``EmulationMxfp8LinearKernel``, which dequantizes at load and runs a plain\n  BF16 linear.\n\nWhy dequantize instead of writing a Triton FP8 GEMM: on gfx90a a Triton FP8\nw8a8 ``tl.dot`` GEMM reaches only ~7-21 TFLOPS (the FP8 operands have to be\nupconverted anyway), while a BF16 ``torch.mm`` reaches ~103-133 TFLOPS. Keeping\nthe weights in FP8 to save memory would therefore cost ~5x in dense-GEMM speed,\nwhich is a bad trade: only *dense* linears take this path (MoE experts keep\ntheir own Triton FP8 kernels), so the 1-byte -> 2-byte growth is bounded by the\nnon-expert parameter count (~10 GB for a 397B/512-expert MoE, i.e. ~1.3 GB per\nGPU at TP=8).\n\nAccuracy: the FP8 (E4M3) -> BF16 cast is exact -- E4M3's 3+1 mantissa bits and\n4-bit exponent both fit in BF16 -- so the only error added versus a true scaled\nGEMM is one BF16 rounding of the dequantized weight (~2^-9 relative) against\n~2^-4 intrinsic FP8 weight-quantization error. The activation is additionally\nNOT re-quantized to FP8 (it stays BF16), which removes the activation-quant\nerror term the FP8 path would have had.\n\nOpt out with ``VLLM_DISABLED_KERNELS=FP8W8A8EmulationLinearKernel``.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\nfrom torch.nn.parameter import Parameter\n\nfrom vllm.logger import init_logger\nfrom vllm.model_executor.layers.fusion.quant_activation import (\n    QuantizedActivation,\n)\nfrom vllm.model_executor.utils import replace_parameter\nfrom vllm.platforms import current_platform\n\nfrom .ScaledMMLinearKernel import (\n    FP8ScaledMMLinearKernel,\n    FP8ScaledMMLinearLayerConfig,\n)\n\nlogger = init_logger(__name__)\n\n_FP8_DTYPES = (\n    torch.float8_e4m3fn,\n    torch.float8_e4m3fnuz,\n    torch.float8_e5m2,\n    torch.float8_e5m2fnuz,\n)\n\n\ndef rocm_lacks_hardware_fp8() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True on AMD CDNA1/CDNA2 GPUs: no FP8 MMA, no ``torch._scaled_mm``.\"\"\"\n    if not current_platform.is_rocm():\n        return False\n\n    from vllm.platforms.rocm import get_cdna_version, on_cdna\n\n    # get_cdna_version(): gfx908 -> 1, gfx90a -> 2, gfx942 -> 3, gfx950 -> 4.\n    # Hardware FP8 (and hence hipBLASLt FP8 scaled-mm) starts at CDNA3.\n    return on_cdna() and get_cdna_version() < 3\n\n\nclass FP8W8A8EmulationLinearKernel(FP8ScaledMMLinearKernel):\n    \"\"\"FP8 w8a8 dense linear via load-time dequant, for GPUs without FP8 HW.\"\"\"\n\n    # Accumulated over all rewritten layers, for one informational log line.\n    _fp8_bytes = 0\n    _dq_bytes = 0\n\n    @classmethod\n    def is_supported(\n        cls, compute_capability: int | None = None\n    ) -> tuple[bool, str | None]:\n        if not rocm_lacks_hardware_fp8():\n            return False, (\n                \"is only used on pre-MI300 ROCm GPUs, which have no hardware \"\n                \"FP8 and no torch._scaled_mm support.\"\n            )\n        return True, None\n\n    @classmethod\n    def can_implement(cls, c: FP8ScaledMMLinearLayerConfig) -> tuple[bool, str | None]:\n        if c.weight_quant_key.scale.group_shape.is_per_group():\n            return False, \"cannot implement block/group-wise FP8 weights.\"\n        out_dtype = c.out_dtype or torch.get_default_dtype()\n        if not out_dtype.is_floating_point or out_dtype.itemsize < 2:\n            return False, f\"requires a >= 2-byte floating point output dtype.\"\n        return True, None\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _as_nk(weight: torch.Tensor, layer: torch.nn.Module) -> torch.Tensor:\n        \"\"\"Return ``weight`` oriented as [N, K] (out_features, in_features).\n\n        Quant methods leave the prepared parameter transposed to [K, N] and\n        tag it with ``input_dim=0`` / ``output_dim=1``; prefer that contract\n        over guessing from strides.\n        \"\"\"\n        if weight.dim() != 2:\n            return weight\n        input_dim = getattr(weight, \"input_dim\", None)\n        if input_dim == 0:\n            return weight.t()\n        if input_dim == 1:\n            return weight\n        # No dim tags: fall back to the layout the compressed-tensors schemes\n        # produce (transposed view => stride(0) == 1).\n        if weight.stride(0) == 1 and weight.stride(1) != 1:\n            return weight.t()\n        return weight\n\n    def _dequant(\n        self, weight: torch.Tensor, weight_scale: torch.Tensor | None, layer: torch.nn.Module\n    ) -> torch.Tensor:\n        \"\"\"Dequantize an FP8 [N, K] weight, returning a float32 [N, K] tensor.\"\"\"\n        w_nk = self._as_nk(weight, layer)\n        if w_nk.stride(-1) != 1:\n            w_nk = w_nk.contiguous()\n        n, k = w_nk.shape\n        w_f32 = w_nk.to(torch.float32)\n\n        if weight_scale is None or weight_scale.numel() == 1:\n            scale = (\n                1.0\n                if weight_scale is None\n                else weight_scale.to(torch.float32).reshape(-1)[0]\n            )\n            return w_f32 * scale\n\n        scale = weight_scale.to(torch.float32).reshape(-1)\n        if scale.numel() == n:\n            return w_f32 * scale.unsqueeze(1)\n        if scale.numel() == k:\n            return w_f32 * scale.unsqueeze(0)\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"FP8 emulation: weight_scale with {scale.numel()} elements \"\n            f\"matches neither N={n} nor K={k}.\"\n        )\n\n    def process_weights_after_loading(self, layer: torch.nn.Module) -> None:\n        weight, weight_scale, _, _ = self._get_layer_params(layer)\n        if weight is None or weight.dtype not in _FP8_DTYPES:\n            # Already dequantized by an earlier pass, or never FP8 at all.\n            return\n\n        out_dtype = self.config.out_dtype or torch.get_default_dtype()\n        w_dq = self._dequant(weight, weight_scale, layer).to(out_dtype)\n\n        self.__class__._fp8_bytes += weight.numel() * weight.element_size()\n        self.__class__._dq_bytes += w_dq.numel() * w_dq.element_size()\n        logger.info_once(\n            \"Emulating FP8 w8a8 dense linears with %s GEMM on this GPU (no \"\n            \"hardware FP8 and no torch._scaled_mm support): dequantizing \"\n            \"weights at load time. So far %.2f GiB of FP8 weights -> %.2f GiB.\",\n            str(out_dtype).replace(\"torch.\", \"\"),\n            self.__class__._fp8_bytes / 2**30,\n            self.__class__._dq_bytes / 2**30,\n            scope=\"global\",\n        )\n\n        # Store as a [N, K] parameter so apply_weights can call F.linear\n        # directly; the weight loader has already run.\n        replace_parameter(layer, \"weight\", Parameter(w_dq, requires_grad=False))\n        layer.weight.input_dim = 1\n        layer.weight.output_dim = 0\n\n    def apply_weights(\n        self,\n        layer: torch.nn.Module,\n        x: torch.Tensor | QuantizedActivation,\n        bias: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n    ) -> torch.Tensor:\n        if isinstance(x, QuantizedActivation):\n            # Defensive only: this kernel does not advertise input_quant_key(),\n            # so manual fusion never hands us a pre-quantized activation.\n            x = (x.data.to(torch.float32) * x.scale).to(x.orig_dtype).view(\n                *x.orig_shape\n            )\n\n        weight = layer.weight\n        if weight.dtype in _FP8_DTYPES:\n            # Not pre-dequantized (process_weights_after_loading was skipped):\n            # dequantize on the fly so we never reach torch._scaled_mm.\n            _, weight_scale, _, _ = self._get_layer_params(layer)\n            weight = self._dequant(weight, weight_scale, layer)\n\n        # F.linear needs matching dtypes; .to() is a no-op when they already do.\n        return torch.nn.functional.linear(x, weight.to(x.dtype), bias).to(x.dtype)\n\n    def apply_scaled_mm(self, **kwargs) -> torch.Tensor:\n        # This kernel overrides apply_weights and must never call\n        # torch._scaled_mm, which does not exist on pre-MI300 ROCm.\n        raise NotImplementedError(\n            \"FP8W8A8EmulationLinearKernel dequantizes and runs F.linear; \"\n            \"apply_scaled_mm is intentionally not implemented.\"\n        )\n"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d8d162a-aacb-49eb-8d41-ca88b571bdc8","uuid":"2dae08a7-c1c7-4a3b-877d-a3e070cdd3df"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_a08f65868bb631d5","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8/20260915T150443Z-6b7d597b/runs/specialist/38272543d24d40a5ad7455d3b42904f2/wt2/pkg/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/scaled_mm/emulation.py has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d8d162a-aacb-49eb-8d41-ca88b571bdc8","uuid":"5d26b288-e48e-48c5-8a72-b43c29ed79d3","timestamp":"2026-09-15T15:45:58.790Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8/20260915T150443Z-6b7d597b/runs/specialist/38272543d24d40a5ad7455d3b42904f2/wt2/pkg/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/scaled_mm/emulation.py","content":"# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project\n\n\"\"\"FP8 w8a8 dense-linear emulation for AMD GPUs without hardware FP8.\n\n``torch._scaled_mm`` hard-rejects FP8 inputs on ROCm devices older than MI300\n(\"torch._scaled_mm is only supported on CUDA devices with compute capability\n>= 9.0 or 8.9, or ROCm MI300+\"). CDNA1/CDNA2 parts (gfx908 / gfx90a, e.g.\nMI250X) have no FP8 matrix instruction at all, so *no* scaled-mm provider can\nserve an FP8 checkpoint there. Before this kernel existed, the pre-MI300 ROCm\nFP8 registry fell through the aiter / skinny-GEMM / rowwise gates (all correctly\narch-gated) and landed on ``ChannelWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel``, whose\n``compute capability >= 89`` gate is fooled by gfx90a reporting capability\n``(9, 0)`` -- so the engine aborted inside ``profile_run``.\n\nThis kernel bridges the gap: it dequantizes the FP8 weight to the activation\ndtype ONCE at load time and then runs a plain ``F.linear``. That is the same\nrecipe already used in-tree by\n\n* ``model_executor/layers/quantization/fp8.py`` -- the ``VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT``\n  per-tensor / per-channel path (\"dequant to BF16 and run GEMM\"), and\n* ``model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/emulation.py`` --\n  ``EmulationMxfp8LinearKernel``, which dequantizes at load and runs a plain\n  BF16 linear.\n\nWhy dequantize instead of writing a Triton FP8 GEMM: on gfx90a a Triton FP8\nw8a8 ``tl.dot`` GEMM reaches only ~7-21 TFLOPS (the FP8 operands have to be\nupconverted anyway), while a BF16 ``torch.mm`` reaches ~103-133 TFLOPS. Keeping\nthe weights in FP8 to save memory would therefore cost ~5x in dense-GEMM speed,\nwhich is a bad trade: only *dense* linears take this path (MoE experts keep\ntheir own Triton FP8 kernels), so the 1-byte -> 2-byte growth is bounded by the\nnon-expert parameter count (~10 GB for a 397B/512-expert MoE, i.e. ~1.3 GB per\nGPU at TP=8).\n\nAccuracy: the FP8 (E4M3) -> BF16 cast is exact -- E4M3's 3+1 mantissa bits and\n4-bit exponent both fit in BF16 -- so the only error added versus a true scaled\nGEMM is one BF16 rounding of the dequantized weight (~2^-9 relative) against\n~2^-4 intrinsic FP8 weight-quantization error. The activation is additionally\nNOT re-quantized to FP8 (it stays BF16), which removes the activation-quant\nerror term the FP8 path would have had.\n\nOpt out with ``VLLM_DISABLED_KERNELS=FP8W8A8EmulationLinearKernel``.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\nfrom torch.nn.parameter import Parameter\n\nfrom vllm.logger import init_logger\nfrom vllm.model_executor.layers.fusion.quant_activation import (\n    QuantizedActivation,\n)\nfrom vllm.model_executor.utils import replace_parameter\nfrom vllm.platforms import current_platform\n\nfrom .ScaledMMLinearKernel import (\n    FP8ScaledMMLinearKernel,\n    FP8ScaledMMLinearLayerConfig,\n)\n\nlogger = init_logger(__name__)\n\n_FP8_DTYPES = (\n    torch.float8_e4m3fn,\n    torch.float8_e4m3fnuz,\n    torch.float8_e5m2,\n    torch.float8_e5m2fnuz,\n)\n\n\ndef rocm_lacks_hardware_fp8() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True on AMD CDNA1/CDNA2 GPUs: no FP8 MMA, no ``torch._scaled_mm``.\"\"\"\n    if not current_platform.is_rocm():\n        return False\n\n    from vllm.platforms.rocm import get_cdna_version, on_cdna\n\n    # get_cdna_version(): gfx908 -> 1, gfx90a -> 2, gfx942 -> 3, gfx950 -> 4.\n    # Hardware FP8 (and hence hipBLASLt FP8 scaled-mm) starts at CDNA3.\n    return on_cdna() and get_cdna_version() < 3\n\n\nclass FP8W8A8EmulationLinearKernel(FP8ScaledMMLinearKernel):\n    \"\"\"FP8 w8a8 dense linear via load-time dequant, for GPUs without FP8 HW.\"\"\"\n\n    # Accumulated over all rewritten layers, for one informational log line.\n    _fp8_bytes = 0\n    _dq_bytes = 0\n\n    @classmethod\n    def is_supported(\n        cls, compute_capability: int | None = None\n    ) -> tuple[bool, str | None]:\n        if not rocm_lacks_hardware_fp8():\n            return False, (\n                \"is only used on pre-MI300 ROCm GPUs, which have no hardware \"\n                \"FP8 and no torch._scaled_mm support.\"\n            )\n        return True, None\n\n    @classmethod\n    def can_implement(cls, c: FP8ScaledMMLinearLayerConfig) -> tuple[bool, str | None]:\n        if c.weight_quant_key.scale.group_shape.is_per_group():\n            return False, \"cannot implement block/group-wise FP8 weights.\"\n        out_dtype = c.out_dtype or torch.get_default_dtype()\n        if not out_dtype.is_floating_point or out_dtype.itemsize < 2:\n            return False, f\"requires a >= 2-byte floating point output dtype.\"\n        return True, None\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _as_nk(weight: torch.Tensor, layer: torch.nn.Module) -> torch.Tensor:\n        \"\"\"Return ``weight`` oriented as [N, K] (out_features, in_features).\n\n        Quant methods leave the prepared parameter transposed to [K, N] and\n        tag it with ``input_dim=0`` / ``output_dim=1``; prefer that contract\n        over guessing from strides.\n        \"\"\"\n        if weight.dim() != 2:\n            return weight\n        input_dim = getattr(weight, \"input_dim\", None)\n        if input_dim == 0:\n            return weight.t()\n        if input_dim == 1:\n            return weight\n        # No dim tags: fall back to the layout the compressed-tensors schemes\n        # produce (transposed view => stride(0) == 1).\n        if weight.stride(0) == 1 and weight.stride(1) != 1:\n            return weight.t()\n        return weight\n\n    def _dequant(\n        self, weight: torch.Tensor, weight_scale: torch.Tensor | None, layer: torch.nn.Module\n    ) -> torch.Tensor:\n        \"\"\"Dequantize an FP8 [N, K] weight, returning a float32 [N, K] tensor.\"\"\"\n        w_nk = self._as_nk(weight, layer)\n        if w_nk.stride(-1) != 1:\n            w_nk = w_nk.contiguous()\n        n, k = w_nk.shape\n        w_f32 = w_nk.to(torch.float32)\n\n        if weight_scale is None or weight_scale.numel() == 1:\n            scale = (\n                1.0\n                if weight_scale is None\n                else weight_scale.to(torch.float32).reshape(-1)[0]\n            )\n            return w_f32 * scale\n\n        scale = weight_scale.to(torch.float32).reshape(-1)\n        if scale.numel() == n:\n            return w_f32 * scale.unsqueeze(1)\n        if scale.numel() == k:\n            return w_f32 * scale.unsqueeze(0)\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"FP8 emulation: weight_scale with {scale.numel()} elements \"\n            f\"matches neither N={n} nor K={k}.\"\n        )\n\n    def process_weights_after_loading(self, layer: torch.nn.Module) -> None:\n        weight, weight_scale, _, _ = self._get_layer_params(layer)\n        if weight is None or weight.dtype not in _FP8_DTYPES:\n            # Already dequantized by an earlier pass, or never FP8 at all.\n            return\n\n        out_dtype = self.config.out_dtype or torch.get_default_dtype()\n        w_dq = self._dequant(weight, weight_scale, layer).to(out_dtype)\n\n        self.__class__._fp8_bytes += weight.numel() * weight.element_size()\n        self.__class__._dq_bytes += w_dq.numel() * w_dq.element_size()\n        logger.info_once(\n            \"Emulating FP8 w8a8 dense linears with %s GEMM on this GPU (no \"\n            \"hardware FP8 and no torch._scaled_mm support): dequantizing \"\n            \"weights at load time. So far %.2f GiB of FP8 weights -> %.2f GiB.\",\n            str(out_dtype).replace(\"torch.\", \"\"),\n            self.__class__._fp8_bytes / 2**30,\n            self.__class__._dq_bytes / 2**30,\n            scope=\"global\",\n        )\n\n        # Store as a [N, K] parameter so apply_weights can call F.linear\n        # directly; the weight loader has already run.\n        replace_parameter(layer, \"weight\", Parameter(w_dq, requires_grad=False))\n        layer.weight.input_dim = 1\n        layer.weight.output_dim = 0\n\n    def apply_weights(\n        self,\n        layer: torch.nn.Module,\n        x: torch.Tensor | QuantizedActivation,\n        bias: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n    ) -> torch.Tensor:\n        if isinstance(x, QuantizedActivation):\n            # Defensive only: this kernel does not advertise input_quant_key(),\n            # so manual fusion never hands us a pre-quantized activation.\n            x = (x.data.to(torch.float32) * x.scale).to(x.orig_dtype).view(\n                *x.orig_shape\n            )\n\n        weight = layer.weight\n        if weight.dtype in _FP8_DTYPES:\n            # Not pre-dequantized (process_weights_after_loading was skipped):\n            # dequantize on the fly so we never reach torch._scaled_mm.\n            _, weight_scale, _, _ = self._get_layer_params(layer)\n            weight = self._dequant(weight, weight_scale, layer)\n\n        # F.linear needs matching dtypes; .to() is a no-op when they already do.\n        return torch.nn.functional.linear(x, weight.to(x.dtype), bias).to(x.dtype)\n\n    def apply_scaled_mm(self, **kwargs) -> torch.Tensor:\n        # This kernel overrides apply_weights and must never call\n        # torch._scaled_mm, which does not exist on pre-MI300 ROCm.\n        raise NotImplementedError(\n            \"FP8W8A8EmulationLinearKernel dequantizes and runs F.linear; \"\n            \"apply_scaled_mm is intentionally not implemented.\"\n        )\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":34,"newStart":1,"newLines":43,"lines":[" # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0"," # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project"," ","-\"\"\"FP8 w8a8 linear emulation for AMD GPUs that lack hardware FP8.","+\"\"\"FP8 w8a8 dense-linear emulation for AMD GPUs without hardware FP8."," "," ``torch._scaled_mm`` hard-rejects FP8 inputs on ROCm devices older than MI300"," (\"torch._scaled_mm is only supported on CUDA devices with compute capability","->= 9.0 or 8.9, or ROCm MI300+\"). CDNA1/CDNA2 parts (gfx908/gfx90a, e.g. MI250X)","-have no FP8 matrix instruction at all, so *no* scaled-mm provider can serve an","-FP8 checkpoint there: the pre-MI300 ROCm kernel registry fell through every","-aiter/skinny/rowwise gate and landed on","-``ChannelWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel``, which aborted inside","-``profile_run``.","+>= 9.0 or 8.9, or ROCm MI300+\"). CDNA1/CDNA2 parts (gfx908 / gfx90a, e.g.","+MI250X) have no FP8 matrix instruction at all, so *no* scaled-mm provider can","+serve an FP8 checkpoint there. Before this kernel existed, the pre-MI300 ROCm","+FP8 registry fell through the aiter / skinny-GEMM / rowwise gates (all correctly","+arch-gated) and landed on ``ChannelWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel``, whose","+``compute capability >= 89`` gate is fooled by gfx90a reporting capability","+``(9, 0)`` -- so the engine aborted inside ``profile_run``."," ","-This kernel bridges that gap by dequantizing the FP8 weight to the activation","-dtype ONCE at load time and then running a plain ``F.linear`` -- the same","+This kernel bridges the gap: it dequantizes the FP8 weight to the activation","+dtype ONCE at load time and then runs a plain ``F.linear``. That is the same"," recipe already used in-tree by",